# Keep the Docker build context lean and secret-free. The web image builds with
# the repo root as context; without this, every service's node_modules, .git, and
# any local .env would be shipped to the daemon (slow, and a leak risk).
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/mobile-out
# Generated Prisma clients are BUILD OUTPUT, and they carry a platform-specific query
# engine binary. Shipping a developer's copy into the build context risked baking a
# Windows or macOS engine into an Alpine image — and, now that postinstall skips a
# generate whose schema hash already matches (audit CI-3), it could even be *believed*.
# The image generates its own, always.
**/prisma/generated
.git
.github
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.production.example
**/coverage
**/*.log
docs
test
